{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>His eyes are darkened, etc.</b> It intends along the lines of the verse's saying (Psalms 68:7): ״מוֹצִיא אֲסִירִים בַּכּוֹשָׁרוֹת״, which our Sages of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah ch. 3) expounded as בְּכִי וְשִׁירוֹת — weeping for Egypt and songs for Israel. This is the meaning of His saying <b>חַכְלִילִי עֵינַיִם</b> — in the language of redness, which is the matter of judgments, for all redness indicates the severity of the sentence, as blood upon blood has been reached. And He said <b>מִיָּיִן</b> — meaning from the source of judgment, which is wine. Or it may allude that the cause of vengeance is from wine — meaning, on account of the suffering and transgression that the enemies of Torah inflicted upon the people of learning. My heart, my heart, over this matter; my innards, my innards, over that the children of iniquity have prevented us from occupying ourselves with the Torah of El Hai — and for this He will take vengeance with the arousal of the intensification of judgments. And at that time itself <b>and white of teeth from milk</b> — He will show us the whiteness of teeth from milk. Or perhaps it alludes, in His saying ״וּלְבֶן״, to Israel, whom HaShem called בֵּן, as it is written (Jeremiah 31:20): ״הֲבֵן יַקִּיר לִי״. And His saying <b>מֵחָלָב</b> is the aspect of חֶסֶד and compassion which our Father will arouse upon us at that time itself, when He is the avenger of vengeance, and this is what is said (Micah 7:15): ״כִּימֵי צֵאתְךָ״, etc. — just as then there was weeping and songs, so too shall it be, speedily in our days, Amen."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The translation renders the Hebrew wordplay 'לִבִּי לִבִּי… מֵעַי מֵעַי' literally with repeated English nouns to preserve the rhetorical repetition. The phrase 'בְּנֵי תּוֹרָה' is rendered as 'the people of learning' and 'בְּנֵי עַוְלָה' as 'the children of iniquity,' maintaining the parallelism."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:41.582464320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}